And there you go.

00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:01.850
Here is our Lego chicken
image in our Multi-Regional US

00:21:01.850 --> 00:21:02.450
bucket.

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:03.530
It's as simple as that--

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:05.444
a few steps to get
your data into GCS.

00:21:05.444 --> 00:21:07.860
And once your data is there,
you can serve it to content--

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:10.151
or you can serve it to your
users throughout the globe,

00:21:10.151 --> 00:21:12.110
or expose it to any
other services that

00:21:12.110 --> 00:21:14.220
are available from
Google Cloud platform.

00:21:14.220 --> 00:21:18.110
Now, I mentioned
I wanted to show

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:19.790
one of the unique
differentiators that

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:23.030
comes from GCS, that global
built-in edge-caching

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:24.290
that we do.

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:28.730
So it's really hard for me to
simulate a user at this point

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:31.460
in time requesting data
from London, for instance,

00:21:31.460 --> 00:21:32.580
from here.

00:21:32.580 --> 00:21:36.200
So what I can do is I could
show you us requesting data

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:39.640
from a bucket that's perhaps
a Multi-Regional bucket

00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:41.190
in the EU.

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:44.510
So I'll go back to
my storage browser.

00:21:44.510 --> 00:21:47.240
And you can see I have various
buckets in various locations

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:48.320
throughout the globe.

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:52.680
I will go to this
Chris's EU bucket.

00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:55.589
In it, I have our
