00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:55.530
So a massive, massive difference
in how fast a user would really

00:22:55.530 --> 00:22:57.960
get that content, because
Google is essentially

00:22:57.960 --> 00:23:00.750
trying to push it as close
as possible to me requesting

00:23:00.750 --> 00:23:02.530
that information from you.

00:23:02.530 --> 00:23:07.350
So for you, as customers of
GCS, whether you're in Tokyo,

00:23:07.350 --> 00:23:10.080
or you have users in Tokyo,
or London, or Mumbai,

00:23:10.080 --> 00:23:12.840
we're basically going to try
to give those users requesting

00:23:12.840 --> 00:23:15.745
your content the best experience
possible for content serving.

00:23:15.745 --> 00:23:17.370
KIRILL TROPIN: Yeah,
that's phenomenal.

00:23:17.370 --> 00:23:19.203
And it was a 1 megabyte
object or something.

00:23:19.203 --> 00:23:21.830
CHRIS TALBOTT: Yeah, it
was a pretty big object.

00:23:21.830 --> 00:23:23.595
The Lego chicken
